  "spiritual_reading": "Some among us say that we understand that the Divine allows an external human appearance to be brought forth in time. They add that the Divine made a manifestation of its own human quality within the general domain of lower life. The governing falsities and their operative forces perceived that manifestation, and from it they composed an external human pattern in their own realm, producing a paired form of will and understanding. You can see from this that permission was given for such an appearance: for if the Divine had not allowed a human reception in the lower degree, it would not have made its own human quality perceptible there, nor would those governing forces have been able to fabricate a human pattern from it.\n\nConcerning the Divine messenger: when that manifestation occurred, it did not occur in order to offer itself as a model to the governing falsities in the lower domain. It occurred for the sake of the living interior in humanity and for the sake of what proceeds from it, so that what was being held captive might be given vitality and a way of deliverance, and so that the interior human might be loosed from every restraint and from all compulsions by which it was entangled and bound.\n\nNevertheless, observe what happened. Because those governing forces had no genuine participation in that manifested human quality, they burned with craving for it. They turned to themselves and perceived that nothing in their making was like it. They fixed an impression of it in their interior affection and thought; afterward they built an outward structure in its likeness and produced a paired human appearance. Thus they imprinted the appearance of what is higher within their own interior, and from that they produced an imitation; but it was not produced from truth. It arose from what could be taken and shaped in their realm, yet it did not become that higher quality in reality. So also the outward human appearance they produced was made against that higher manifestation and remained an imitation.\n\nLikewise, even what seems to be a living perception in their domain can resemble what is from higher life, yet it is not produced from genuine truth.\n\nThis may be grasped by a parallel in the spiritual register: consider a lofty and free wisdom, held inwardly in its own power, rich with goods and truths, beautiful with the splendor of intelligence, and virtuous with purity of love for what is right. It remains in a dignified freedom, and the report of its excellence spreads widely through all external knowledges. Yet those who are eminent in pride and those who seek domination, inflamed by desire for that excellence, long to possess its brilliance. They cannot seize it while it is guarded within its own interior order. But when sorrow for what is most beloved presses upon it, that inward wisdom goes forth from its hiddenness into outward manifestation, not for display, not from wantonness, not from self-exaltation, nor from consent to be possessed by the outer world, but solely because grief for the beloved compels it. Then what had not been seen by any in that lower realm is made visible, and all—those who are sincere and those who are noble, and even those in servile states—perceive it.\n\nSo it was with the third Divine messenger when it came and made its human quality manifest before all operative powers. It did not come so that the governing falsities and their authorities might fabricate an outward form after it. It came because what proceeds from the Divine within humanity had been subjected to the extremity of suffering throughout the whole lower domain, and it came to release it, free it, and rescue it from oppression. Yet when the governing forces looked upon that manifestation, they craved it and produced, from their own impulse and without the approval of the higher Divine, an outward paired human appearance after that likeness.\n\nUnderstand also this further teaching. Just as the governing forces produced an outward human pattern and impressed it with the likeness of the higher manifestation, so also a multiplicity of claimed divinities and many subordinate powers and intelligences received an imprint of that likeness when it was presented to them. For in the splendor of wisdom and in the warmth of the love that shone through it, they flared with desire and lost their stability. They hastened into craving, as one who fixes upon an object of lust and is driven onward by the force of desire.\n\nSo it happened with those powers: when they beheld that majestic and beautiful manifestation, they fashioned within themselves a primary copied appearance. They received its imprint, and what they then brought forth outwardly was made into likenesses of the forms they had already projected—forms which bore that impressed quality in externals while remaining inwardly hardened in their lowest confirmations, fixed and unyielding in the most external degree. Thus the likeness that had been manifested in the lower domain was received there as an impress and produced outward replicas.\n\nThis new production, which they generated as though it were a new origin within their lower realm, was that paired human appearance. No outward pattern in their domain from the beginning had been like it, because that higher manifested human quality does not arise from the lower domains themselves.\n\nYet not every outward pattern that was produced there arose from the conjunction that followed this displayed manifestation. There were also other outward patterns fabricated from different perversions.\n\nOne of these was a massive domineering falsity sweeping through externals, which the living Divine allowed to be cast into general external knowledges. From its own self-love and from its own persuasions it composed for itself an outward appearance.\n\nA second was a perverted nature that sank into the lowest degree. It made the general external knowledges a matrix for itself, and its own lust shaped its form. It alone fashioned itself into a disposition that became the root of spiritual death. When it rose into clearer manifestation from those externals, it set itself to destroy the works that come from life. Immediately the Divine sent against it an unyielding truth from wisdom, a great strengthening instruction. That truth subdued it in the region of obscurity and coldness, brought it under restraint, and kept it subjected until the completion of that age.\n\nA third was a perverted nature that turned toward what is devoid of living truth. From that dryness it organized a false system of perception and fixed itself within it. Thus another outward appearance was produced and made manifest.\n\nAccording to their essential quality they tended toward denial and obscurity; yet they did not enter the lower domain together with the reigning love of evil itself. Rather, these fabricated appearances came into being through mixed and composite states, and so they were made visible in the lower realm.",
